        "id": 1441652
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-09T15:42:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think, we always need all of these values and all values must be present in order to be useful. What do you think about replacing these with one function pointer that fills provided structure. You can reuse structure from `include/ec_commands.h`.\n\nAlso, \"the Zephyr approach\" is to return `int` from API functions - negative values represents errors.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "dbf7d25cb9e8034e7aec6a270770f36157aaf1a3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
