        "id": 1441652
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-09T15:42:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This assumes that the SDCP claim is available at some address, which is a SoC/platform implementation detail. I theorize about some bootloader that gives us a callback to get claim (and/or operate on `sk_f`).\n\nI would move `memcpy()` to platform part. Also, there is no need to expose address as Kconfig options.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 8,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "dbf7d25cb9e8034e7aec6a270770f36157aaf1a3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
